# ssh-import

## cli
- label: `ssh` is a second `import` source alongside cursor-cloud — bin/tracequest.js still routes case "import" to cmdImport, which lazy-loads src/import/ssh-import.js for source ssh the same way it lazy-loads cursor-cloud-import.js, a missing positional source dies (exit 1, cli-die) naming both cursor-cloud and ssh, and an unrecognised source dies naming both
  id: sshim
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'import with an unknown source dies|import help lists usage and options|import ssh with no hosts dies' test/bin/tracequest-cursor-cloud-import-integration.test.js test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]
- label: `tracequest import ssh` takes remaining positionals as OpenSSH destinations, and when none are given it reads HOME/.tracequest/import-hosts (one host per line, blank lines and # comments skipped); if that file is absent or yields no hosts the command dies (exit 1) with an actionable message naming both the positional form and the import-hosts file
  id: sshho
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'import ssh with no hosts dies|import ssh reads hosts from the import-hosts file' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]
- label: import ssh options are [--dry-run] [--full] [-i/--identity <file>] [--port <N>] [--as <id>] [-h/--help], declared in bin/tracequest.js's import parseArgs, listed in the import Options help block, and ignored by the cursor-cloud route; --port is the SSH port (a positive integer) and --identity is the SSH identity file (rejected when the path contains whitespace)
  id: sshopt
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'import help lists usage and options|import ssh rejects a non-integer --port|import ssh rejects an identity path with whitespace' test/bin/tracequest-cursor-cloud-import-integration.test.js test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js && sed -n '/case "import"/,/break;/p' bin/tracequest.js | grep -q 'identity'
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]
- label: `tracequest import ssh <host> --dry-run` performs the same rsync planning as a real run (including fixture-mode local rsync) but writes no session files and creates no directories under the hosts root, prints one planned action per source tree, and a subsequent real run starts from an unchanged local state
  id: sshdry
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'dry-run prints planned actions and writes nothing under the hosts root' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]
- label: `tracequest import ssh --full` is the escape hatch that passes rsync --ignore-times so every remote file is reconsidered even when size and mtime match, composing with --dry-run, and the flag stays the shared import --full already declared for cursor-cloud
  id: sshfu
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'full recopies a remote tree whose size and mtime still match' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]
- label: every import ssh run ends with a one-line summary reporting six counts in the order checked, fetched, imported, updated, skipped, failed — checked is the number of (host, source) pairs, fetched is how many of those actually invoked rsync rather than being skipped as absent on the remote, imported/updated/skipped/failed are those pairs' write outcomes, the process exits 0 when failed is 0 and exits 1 when any pair failed
  id: sshsm
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'summary reports checked, fetched, imported, updated, skipped, and failed counts' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]
- label: a long import never looks hung — for each host the importer prints a plan line naming how many of the six source trees will be fetched, skipped as unchanged, or skipped as absent BEFORE rsyncing that host, and every per-source action line (import, update, skip) is emitted as that tree is decided
  id: sshpr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'prints a per-host plan before rsyncing that host' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]
- label: sessions materialised by `import ssh` flow through the normal pipeline with no extra flag or rescan command — findSessions discovers them with their original source (claude/cursor/codex/factory/grok) plus host, buildIndex indexes them, and search returns hits whose source is the original agent source
  id: sshis
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'imported ssh sessions are indexed and searchable with original source and host' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]

## transport
- label: a missing remote source tree is skip-with-warning, never fatal — the importer prints a warning naming the host and source, counts the pair under skipped, and continues; any other per-pair rsync error that is not "remote path missing" counts under failed without aborting the rest of the run
  id: sshsk
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'skips a source tree that is absent on the remote|counts a rsync failure under failed and continues' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]
- label: an unreachable host (ssh non-zero that is not a missing remote path) counts that host's remaining source pairs as failed after the first transport error, continues with the next host, and never prints identity-file contents
  id: sshxp
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'unreachable host fails that host and continues with the next' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]

## materialisation
- label: each host copies the five filesystem session trees plus OpenCode's opencode.db from remote $HOME — .claude/projects, .cursor/projects, .codex/sessions, .factory/sessions, .grok/sessions, .local/share/opencode/opencode.db — and never copies the cursor-cloud import root or credential files outside those session trees
  id: sshly
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'copies the filesystem session trees including opencode and not cursor-cloud' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, sessions, implemented]
- label: re-running import ssh is idempotent — rsync's default size+mtime skip leaves unchanged files' mtime untouched so buildIndex does not re-index them, dest trees that receive no transferred files count as skipped, and the importer never passes --delete so a session that vanished remotely stays in the local archive
  id: sshidm
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 're-run skips unchanged trees and preserves mtime|does not delete a local file that vanished from the fixture' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, sessions, implemented]

## source
- label: ssh import does not add a new KNOWN_SESSION_SOURCE — copied files keep source claude, cursor, codex, factory, or grok so source:claude matches local and imported Claude sessions alike
  id: sshsv
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'imported ssh sessions are indexed and searchable with original source and host' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, sessions, implemented]
- label: findSessions stamps host on any discovery row whose path sits under the resolved hosts root (the first path component after that root), local sessions omit host, sessionToApiObject copies host when present, and list/find --json include host when present
  id: sshst
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'stamps host on sessions under the hosts root|list --json includes host for imported sessions' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, sessions, implemented]
- label: after import ssh, `tracequest serve` GET /api/sessions?expr=host:gpu returns those rows with source equal to the original agent and host equal to the host id, and GET /view?path= of an imported jsonl returns 200 HTML of that session
  id: sshvw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'serve lists host:gpu and opens /view of an imported session' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, serve, implemented]

## tests
- label: `--as <id>` sets the host id independently of the SSH destination when exactly one host is imported, import-hosts lines of the form `user@gpu as gpu` do the same per host, `--as` with more than one host dies (exit 1), and dest trees land under the alias not the raw destination
  id: sshas
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'parseHostRef|--as aliases the host id|import-hosts as alias|--as with multiple hosts dies' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, cli, implemented]

# usage-limits
- label: after copying session trees, import ssh runs the same usage-limits collectors for that host and writes a secret-free snapshot at hosts/{hostId}/.tracequest/usage-limits.json; fixture mode collects from the fixture host HOME with no SSH
  id: sshul
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'import ssh writes a usage-limits snapshot' test/bin/tracequest-usage-limits-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, usage-limits, implemented]
- label: a usage-limits probe/transport error is skip-with-warning and does not increment the six import summary counters (fact sshsm) or abort the rest of the run; --dry-run prints the plan and writes no snapshot
  id: sshuw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'limits skip-with-warning|dry-run does not write usage-limits|summary counters unchanged' test/bin/tracequest-usage-limits-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, ssh-import, usage-limits, implemented]
